Package: vayuayan
Type: Package
Title: Air Quality Data from Indian Monitoring Networks and Satellites
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Saket", "Choudhary", , "saketc@iitb.ac.in", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Mahesh Kumar", "Prajapat", , "22b0433@iitb.ac.in", role = "aut"),
    person("Darakhshan", "Nehal", , "darakhshannehal@gmail.com", role = "ctb")
  )
Description: Downloads and examines air quality data from three sources.
    The Central Pollution Control Board (CPCB) of India operates more than
    600 monitoring stations. Open Air Quality (OAQ) <https://oaq.notf.in>
    collects data from low-cost sensor networks in India. The Atmospheric
    Composition Analysis Group at Washington University in St. Louis gives
    satellite estimates of fine particulate matter (PM2.5) for all areas of
    the Earth <https://www.satpm.org>. The package calculates the CPCB
    National Air Quality Index and the mean PM2.5 in an area.
